<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<model version="NetLogo 7.0.4" snapToGrid="true">
  <code><![CDATA[; ============================================================
; EMERGENT TRAFFIC CONGESTION SIMULATION
; Complex Systems - NetLogo Assignment
; ============================================================


; ============================================================
; BREEDS
; ============================================================

breed [cars car]
breed [traffic-lights traffic-light]


; ============================================================
; GLOBAL VARIABLES
; ============================================================

globals [
  average-speed
  stopped-cars

  traffic-light-state
  light-timer

  congestion-level
  traffic-density

  cars-passed
  queue-length
]


; ============================================================
; CAR VARIABLES
; ============================================================

cars-own [
  speed
  max-car-speed
]


; ============================================================
; SETUP ROAD
; ============================================================

to setup-road

  ; ----------------------------------------------------------
  ; Green environment
  ; ----------------------------------------------------------

  ask patches [
    set pcolor green
  ]


  ; ----------------------------------------------------------
  ; Main road
  ; Two lanes: y = -1 and y = 1
  ; ----------------------------------------------------------

  ask patches with [
    abs pycor <= 2
  ] [
    set pcolor gray
  ]


  ; ----------------------------------------------------------
  ; Yellow lane divider
  ; ----------------------------------------------------------

  ask patches with [
    pycor = 0
  ] [
    set pcolor yellow
  ]

end


; ============================================================
; SETUP CARS
; ============================================================

to setup-cars

  ; Use the built-in car shape
  set-default-shape cars "car"


  ; ----------------------------------------------------------
  ; Calculate how many cars should be placed in each lane
  ; ----------------------------------------------------------

  let cars-per-lane ceiling (number-of-cars / 2)


  ; ----------------------------------------------------------
  ; Calculate spacing so cars are distributed across
  ; the entire road instead of being randomly clustered.
  ; ----------------------------------------------------------

  let spacing 0

  if cars-per-lane > 1 [

    set spacing
      (world-width - 2) / (cars-per-lane - 1)

  ]


  ; ----------------------------------------------------------
  ; Create cars
  ; ----------------------------------------------------------

  create-cars number-of-cars [

    ; --------------------------------------------------------
    ; Appearance
    ; --------------------------------------------------------

    set color one-of [
      red
      blue
      yellow
      orange
      white
    ]

    set size 1.2


    ; --------------------------------------------------------
    ; Determine lane
    ; --------------------------------------------------------

    let car-index who

    let lane-index car-index mod 2

    let position-index floor (car-index / 2)


    ; --------------------------------------------------------
    ; Lane position
    ; --------------------------------------------------------

    let lane-y item lane-index [-1 1]


    ; --------------------------------------------------------
    ; Position car across the road
    ; --------------------------------------------------------

    setxy
      (min-pxcor + 1 + position-index * spacing)
      lane-y


    ; --------------------------------------------------------
    ; Cars move from left to right
    ; --------------------------------------------------------

    set heading 90


    ; --------------------------------------------------------
    ; Initial speed
    ; Start with a positive speed to avoid
    ; artificial stopped cars during setup.
    ; --------------------------------------------------------

    set max-car-speed max-speed

    set speed
      ((0.8 + random-float 0.2) * max-car-speed)

  ]

end


; ============================================================
; SETUP TRAFFIC LIGHT
; ============================================================

to setup-traffic-light

  set-default-shape traffic-lights "circle"


  create-traffic-lights 1 [

    set size 1.8

    set color green

    ; Position above the road
    setxy 0 3

  ]

end


; ============================================================
; UPDATE TRAFFIC LIGHT
; ============================================================

to update-traffic-light

  set light-timer light-timer + 1


  ; ==========================================================
  ; GREEN -> YELLOW
  ; ==========================================================

  if traffic-light-state = "green"
     and light-timer >= light-duration
  [

    set traffic-light-state "yellow"

    set light-timer 0

    ask traffic-lights [
      set color yellow
    ]

  ]


  ; ==========================================================
  ; YELLOW -> RED
  ; ==========================================================

  if traffic-light-state = "yellow"
     and light-timer >= max list 5 (light-duration / 4)
  [

    set traffic-light-state "red"

    set light-timer 0

    ask traffic-lights [
      set color red
    ]

  ]


  ; ==========================================================
  ; RED -> GREEN
  ; ==========================================================

  if traffic-light-state = "red"
     and light-timer >= light-duration
  [

    set traffic-light-state "green"

    set light-timer 0

    ask traffic-lights [
      set color green
    ]

  ]

end


; ============================================================
; MOVE CARS
; ============================================================

to move-cars

  ask cars [

    ; ========================================================
    ; DESIRED SPEED
    ; ========================================================

    let desired-speed max-car-speed


    ; ========================================================
    ; FIND NEAREST CAR AHEAD IN THE SAME LANE
    ; ========================================================

    let current-x xcor
    let current-y ycor


    let cars-ahead other cars with [

      xcor > current-x

      and

      abs (ycor - current-y) < 0.1

    ]


    let car-ahead nobody


    ; Find closest car ahead
    if any? cars-ahead [

      set car-ahead min-one-of cars-ahead [xcor]

    ]


    ; ========================================================
    ; CAR-FOLLOWING BEHAVIOUR
    ; ========================================================

    if car-ahead != nobody [

      let distance-to-car
        ([xcor] of car-ahead - current-x)


      ; ------------------------------------------------------
      ; Very close -> stop
      ; ------------------------------------------------------

      if distance-to-car < safe-distance [

        set desired-speed 0

      ]


      ; ------------------------------------------------------
      ; Moderate distance -> reduce speed smoothly
      ; ------------------------------------------------------

      if distance-to-car >= safe-distance
         and distance-to-car < (safe-distance * 2)
      [

        set desired-speed
          max list 0
          (
            max-car-speed
            *
            (
              distance-to-car
              /
              (safe-distance * 2)
            )
          )

      ]

    ]


    ; ========================================================
    ; TRAFFIC LIGHT BEHAVIOUR
    ; ========================================================


    ; --------------------------------------------------------
    ; RED LIGHT -> STOP
    ; --------------------------------------------------------

    if traffic-light-state = "red"
       and xcor < 0
       and xcor > -8
    [

      set desired-speed 0

    ]


    ; --------------------------------------------------------
    ; YELLOW LIGHT -> SLOW DOWN
    ; --------------------------------------------------------

    if traffic-light-state = "yellow"
       and xcor < 0
       and xcor > -8
    [

      set desired-speed
        min list desired-speed (max-car-speed * 0.5)

    ]


    ; ========================================================
    ; SMOOTH ACCELERATION / DECELERATION
    ; ========================================================

    ifelse speed < desired-speed [

      ; Accelerate smoothly
      set speed
        min list max-car-speed (speed + 0.1)

    ]

    [

      ; Decelerate smoothly
      set speed
        max list desired-speed (speed - 0.2)

    ]


    ; ========================================================
    ; SAFETY LIMITS
    ; ========================================================

    set speed max list 0 speed

    set speed min list max-car-speed speed


    ; ========================================================
    ; MOVE CAR
    ; ========================================================

    fd speed

  ]

end


; ============================================================
; WRAP CARS
; ============================================================

to wrap-cars

  ask cars [

    if xcor > max-pxcor [

      ; Return to beginning of road
      set xcor min-pxcor

      ; Count completed trips
      set cars-passed cars-passed + 1

    ]

  ]

end


; ============================================================
; CALCULATE AVERAGE SPEED
; ============================================================

to calculate-average-speed

  ifelse any? cars [

    set average-speed mean [speed] of cars

  ]

  [

    set average-speed 0

  ]

end


; ============================================================
; COUNT STOPPED CARS
; ============================================================

to calculate-stopped-cars

  set stopped-cars count cars with [
    speed <= 0.05
  ]

end


; ============================================================
; CALCULATE TRAFFIC DENSITY
; ============================================================

to calculate-traffic-density

  ; ----------------------------------------------------------
  ; Road has two lanes.
  ; World width gives the total number of patches across
  ; the road direction.
  ; ----------------------------------------------------------

  let road-capacity 2 * world-width


  ifelse road-capacity > 0 [

    set traffic-density
      (count cars / road-capacity) * 100

  ]

  [

    set traffic-density 0

  ]

end


; ============================================================
; CALCULATE CONGESTION LEVEL
; ============================================================

to calculate-congestion

  ifelse any? cars [

    ; --------------------------------------------------------
    ; Congestion is measured as the percentage of cars
    ; moving below 40% of their maximum speed.
    ; --------------------------------------------------------

    let slow-cars count cars with [
      speed < (0.4 * max-car-speed)
    ]


    set congestion-level
      (slow-cars / count cars) * 100

  ]

  [

    set congestion-level 0

  ]

end


; ============================================================
; CALCULATE QUEUE LENGTH
; ============================================================

to calculate-queue-length

  ; ----------------------------------------------------------
  ; Count stopped cars waiting before the traffic light.
  ; The whole area from the beginning of the road to x = 0
  ; is included.
  ; ----------------------------------------------------------

  set queue-length count cars with [

    xcor < 0
    and
    speed <= 0.05

  ]

end


; ============================================================
; UPDATE ALL STATISTICS
; ============================================================

to update-statistics

  calculate-average-speed

  calculate-stopped-cars

  calculate-traffic-density

  calculate-congestion

  calculate-queue-length

end


; ============================================================
; SETUP
; ============================================================

to setup

  clear-all


  ; ----------------------------------------------------------
  ; Create a wide world automatically.
  ;
  ; X: -50 to 50  -> 101 patches wide
  ; Y: -10 to 10  -> 21 patches high
  ;
  ; This gives enough road capacity for high-density
  ; experiments such as 90 or 100 cars.
  ; ----------------------------------------------------------

  resize-world -50 50 -10 10


  ; ----------------------------------------------------------
  ; Create road
  ; ----------------------------------------------------------

  setup-road


  ; ----------------------------------------------------------
  ; Create cars
  ; ----------------------------------------------------------

  setup-cars


  ; ----------------------------------------------------------
  ; Initial traffic light state
  ; ----------------------------------------------------------

  set traffic-light-state "green"

  set light-timer 0


  ; ----------------------------------------------------------
  ; Create traffic light
  ; ----------------------------------------------------------

  setup-traffic-light


  ; ----------------------------------------------------------
  ; Initialise statistics
  ; ----------------------------------------------------------

  set average-speed 0

  set stopped-cars 0

  set congestion-level 0

  set traffic-density 0

  set cars-passed 0

  set queue-length 0


  ; ----------------------------------------------------------
  ; Calculate initial statistics
  ; ----------------------------------------------------------

  update-statistics


  ; Reset simulation time
  reset-ticks

end


; ============================================================
; MAIN SIMULATION LOOP
; ============================================================

to go

  ; Update traffic signal
  update-traffic-light


  ; Move cars
  move-cars


  ; Wrap cars around the road
  wrap-cars


  ; Update all statistics
  update-statistics


  ; Advance time
  tick

end]]></code>
  <widgets>
    <view x="460" wrappingAllowedX="true" y="5" frameRate="30.0" minPycor="-10" height="335" showTickCounter="true" patchSize="15.8" fontSize="10" wrappingAllowedY="true" width="1599" tickCounterLabel="ticks" maxPycor="10" updateMode="0" maxPxcor="50" minPxcor="-50"></view>
    <slider x="45" step="0.5" y="245" max="5" width="250" display="safe-distance" height="50" min="1" direction="Horizontal" default="1.0" variable="safe-distance"></slider>
    <monitor x="40" precision="17" y="450" height="60" fontSize="11" width="100" display="Cars Passed">cars-passed</monitor>
    <monitor x="160" precision="17" y="385" height="60" fontSize="11" width="100" display="Traffic Light">traffic-light-state</monitor>
    <monitor x="40" precision="17" y="380" height="60" fontSize="11" width="100" display="Congestion %">congestion-level</monitor>
    <monitor x="160" precision="17" y="310" height="60" fontSize="11" width="100" display="Stopped Cars">stopped-cars</monitor>
    <monitor x="40" precision="17" y="310" height="60" fontSize="11" width="100" display="Average Speed">average-speed</monitor>
    <button x="185" y="35" height="40" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="true" kind="Observer" width="55" display="GO">go</button>
    <slider x="45" step="0.1" y="180" max="3" width="250" display="max-speed" height="50" min="0.5" direction="Horizontal" default="3.0" variable="max-speed"></slider>
    <slider x="45" step="1" y="115" max="100" width="250" display="number-of-cars" height="50" min="10" direction="Horizontal" default="100.0" variable="number-of-cars"></slider>
    <button x="105" y="35" height="40" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="55" display="SETUP">setup</button>
    <slider x="165" step="5" y="460" max="60" width="250" display="light-duration" height="50" min="20" direction="Horizontal" default="25.0" variable="light-duration"></slider>
    <monitor x="285" precision="17" y="310" height="60" fontSize="11" width="100" display="Traffic Density (%)">queue-length</monitor>
    <monitor x="285" precision="17" y="385" height="60" fontSize="11" width="100" display="Queue Length">cars-passed</monitor>
  </widgets>
  <info>---

# EMERGENT TRAFFIC CONGESTION SIMULATION

## 1. Overview

This NetLogo model simulates the movement of vehicles on a two-lane road and demonstrates how **traffic congestion can emerge from simple interactions between individual vehicles and a traffic light**.

The model is designed as a **Complex Systems simulation**. Instead of using a central controller to create congestion, each vehicle follows simple local rules based on its surrounding environment. When many vehicles interact with each other, system-level patterns such as traffic queues, slow movement, and congestion emerge.

---

## 2. Objectives

The main objectives of this simulation are:

* To model the movement of vehicles on a road.
* To demonstrate interactions between individual vehicles.
* To simulate vehicle behaviour based on nearby vehicles.
* To model the effect of a traffic light on vehicle movement.
* To demonstrate the emergence of traffic congestion.
* To measure traffic conditions using different performance indicators.
* To demonstrate important Complex Systems concepts such as **agents, local interactions, feedback, emergence, and self-organization**.

---

## 3. Complex System Concepts

This model demonstrates several important concepts of Complex Systems.

### Agents

The main agents in the model are:

* **Cars** – represent individual vehicles.
* **Traffic Light** – controls vehicle movement through different light states.

Each car behaves independently according to the conditions around it.

### Local Interactions

Cars do not need to know the behaviour of every other car in the system.

Instead, each car mainly observes the vehicle directly ahead in the same lane and adjusts its speed according to the distance between them.

### Feedback

The behaviour of one vehicle can affect other vehicles.

For example, when one car slows down, the car behind it may also slow down. This can cause a chain reaction through the traffic.

### Emergence

Traffic congestion is not directly created by the model.

Instead, congestion **emerges from the interactions between individual vehicles and the traffic light**.

Simple vehicle-level rules can therefore produce a complex system-level behaviour.

### Self-Organization

Vehicles automatically form queues when they encounter a red traffic light or slower vehicles.

No central controller tells individual cars where to form a queue.

---

## 4. Model Environment

The simulation contains a **two-lane road**.

The road is represented using different patch colours:

* Green areas represent the surrounding environment.
* Gray areas represent the road.
* A yellow line separates the two lanes.

Vehicles move along the road from left to right.

A traffic light is positioned above the road and controls the movement of vehicles.

---

## 5. Vehicle Behaviour

Each vehicle has its own:

* Current speed
* Maximum speed

During the simulation, each vehicle continuously evaluates the traffic conditions around it.

A vehicle checks whether another vehicle is ahead in the same lane.

If the vehicle ahead is too close, the following vehicle slows down or stops.

If there is enough space, the vehicle can increase its speed.

The model also uses gradual acceleration and deceleration instead of instantly changing the vehicle's speed.

This produces more realistic vehicle movement.

---

## 6. Traffic Light Behaviour

The traffic light has three states:

**Green → Yellow → Red → Green**

### Green

Vehicles are allowed to continue moving.

### Yellow

Vehicles approaching the traffic light reduce their speed.

### Red

Vehicles approaching the traffic light stop and wait.

When multiple vehicles arrive at a red light, they form a queue.

When the light changes back to green, the vehicles gradually start moving again.

---

## 7. Simulation Parameters

The model provides several controls that allow different traffic conditions to be tested.

### Number of Cars

Controls the number of vehicles in the simulation.

Increasing the number of cars can increase interactions and traffic congestion.

### Maximum Speed

Controls the maximum speed that vehicles can reach.

### Safe Distance

Defines the minimum distance that vehicles attempt to maintain from the vehicle ahead.

### Light Duration

Controls how long the traffic light remains in each state before changing.

These parameters allow different traffic scenarios to be investigated.

---

## 8. Measurements and Outputs

The simulation calculates several measurements to evaluate the traffic system.

### Average Speed

Shows the average speed of the vehicles currently in the simulation.

A lower average speed generally indicates heavier traffic conditions.

### Stopped Cars

Shows the number of vehicles that are currently stopped or moving at a very low speed.

### Traffic Density

Represents the number of vehicles relative to the available road capacity.

Higher vehicle density can result in more interactions between cars.

### Congestion %

Shows the percentage of vehicles experiencing significantly reduced speed.

In this model, vehicles travelling below a specified proportion of their maximum speed are considered slow for congestion measurement.

### Traffic Light

Displays the current state of the traffic light:

* Green
* Yellow
* Red

### Queue Length

Shows the number of vehicles waiting in the traffic-light queue.

### Cars Passed

Counts the number of vehicles that successfully complete their movement across the simulated road.

---

## 9. How to Use the Model

Follow these steps to run the simulation:

1. Set the **number-of-cars** slider.
2. Set the **max-speed** slider.
3. Set the **safe-distance** slider.
4. Set the **light-duration** slider.
5. Click the **SETUP** button.
6. Click the **GO** button to start the simulation.
7. Observe the movement of vehicles.
8. Observe how queues form when the traffic light becomes red.
9. Observe how vehicles begin moving when the traffic light becomes green.
10. Monitor the statistics displayed on the interface.

Different parameter values can be tested to observe how traffic conditions change.

---

## 10. Expected Behaviour

When there are fewer vehicles, cars can generally move with fewer interactions and maintain higher speeds.

When the number of vehicles increases, vehicles interact more frequently.

When the traffic light changes to red, vehicles approaching the light stop and form a queue.

As more vehicles join the queue, the number of stopped vehicles and the congestion level can increase.

When the traffic light becomes green, vehicles begin moving again and the queue gradually decreases.

These behaviours demonstrate how local interactions can produce larger system-level traffic patterns.

---

## 11. Emergent Behaviour

The most important feature of this model is **emergent traffic congestion**.

A single vehicle follows relatively simple rules:

* Move forward.
* Maintain a safe distance.
* Slow down when another vehicle is close.
* Stop when necessary.
* Respond to the traffic light.

However, when many vehicles follow these rules simultaneously, complex behaviour emerges.

For example:

**Red Light → Cars Stop → Queue Forms → More Cars Join → Congestion Emerges**

This demonstrates the main idea of a Complex System: **simple individual behaviours can produce complex behaviour at the system level.**

---

## 12. Conclusion

This NetLogo simulation demonstrates how traffic congestion can emerge through the interaction of individual vehicles and a traffic light.

The model shows that complex traffic patterns do not necessarily require complex rules at the individual level.

Through simple rules such as vehicle following, speed adjustment, safe-distance maintenance, and traffic-light response, the model produces system-level behaviours such as:

* Vehicle queues
* Reduced average speed
* Increased stopped vehicles
* Increased traffic density
* Traffic congestion

Therefore, this simulation provides a practical demonstration of **agents, local interactions, feedback, emergence, and self-organization in Complex Systems**.

---

</info>
